diff --git a/kernel/patches/drivers/pci/0028-dt-bindings-PCI-apple-t8010-pcie-Add-the-T8015-variant.patch b/kernel/patches/drivers/pci/0028-dt-bindings-PCI-apple-t8010-pcie-Add-the-T8015-variant.patch
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..b0116878
--- /dev/null
+++ b/kernel/patches/drivers/pci/0028-dt-bindings-PCI-apple-t8010-pcie-Add-the-T8015-variant.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Eduardo Martins <372861+edulmartins@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:40:46 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: pci: apple,t8010-pcie: Add the T8015 variant
+
+The T8015 keeps the four-port H8P/H9P register map but gives each port its
+own NVMMU window (portN and portN-nvmmu) and has no storage port, so its
+NVMe controller is the separate ANS2 block. It therefore has twelve reg
+entries, four port interrupts, and none of the storage-port properties:
+no apple,nvmmu-iova and no apple,nvme-hmb.
+
+Describe that layout in the Apple PCIe binding so the T8015 node can be
+validated. The per-SoC constraints become independent allOf entries so
+the T8010 branch keeps its nine-register and five-interrupt limits and
+the derivative boards still match it.
+
+Signed-off-by: Eduardo Martins <372861+edulmartins@users.noreply.github.com>
+---
+ .../bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml        | 74 ++++++++++++++++---
+ 1 file changed, 63 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml
+index 83db67f..e70f009 100644
+--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml
++++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml
+@@ -4,17 +4,17 @@
+ $id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml#
+ $schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+ 
+-title: Apple S8003, T7000 and T8010 PCIe host controller
++title: Apple S8003, T7000, T8010 and T8015 PCIe host controller
+ 
+ maintainers:
+   - Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
+ 
+ description: |
+-  Apple A9/S8003 (TSMC) and A10/T8010 devices use the H8P/H9P PCIe root
+-  complex for internal storage and Wi-Fi. It exposes one ECAM window shared
+-  by up to four root ports, controller-specific PHY and port register
+-  windows, and a local MSI block. Both SoCs share this register map but
+-  need different power-up and link training sequences.
++  Apple A9/S8003 (TSMC), A10/T8010 and A11/T8015 devices use the H8P/H9P
++  PCIe root complex for internal storage and Wi-Fi. It exposes one ECAM
++  window shared by up to four root ports, controller-specific PHY and port
++  register windows, and a local MSI block. The SoCs share this register map
++  but need different power-up and link training sequences.
+ 
+   The storage port also contains an NVMMU which translates the proprietary
+   Apple ANS FlatDMA format. Unlike a general-purpose IOMMU, this block uses a
+@@ -22,6 +22,10 @@ description: |
+   window. The PCIe driver owns that NVMMU state and exposes it only to the ANS
+   NVMe glue.
+ 
++  The T8015 has no PCIe storage port: its NVMe controller is the separate
++  ANS2 block. Each T8015 root port instead has its own NVMMU window, so the
++  T8015 does not use the storage-port NVMMU properties.
++
+   Apple A8/A8X (T7000/T7001) devices use an earlier version of the same root
+   complex, with the same ECAM layout, port register block and MSI block. It
+   has no separate PHY register windows and no NVMMU, and its reference and
+@@ -65,11 +69,58 @@ allOf:
+         apple,nvmmu-iova: false
+         apple,nvme-hmb: false
+         apple,preinit-phy-port-mask: false
+-    else:
++  - if:
++      properties:
++        compatible:
++          contains:
++            const: apple,t8015-pcie
++    then:
++      properties:
++        reg:
++          minItems: 12
++          maxItems: 12
++        reg-names:
++          items:
++            - const: config
++            - const: port0
++            - const: port0-nvmmu
++            - const: port1
++            - const: port1-nvmmu
++            - const: port2
++            - const: port2-nvmmu
++            - const: port3
++            - const: port3-nvmmu
++            - const: rc
++            - const: phy
++            - const: phy-ip
++        interrupts:
++          minItems: 4
++          maxItems: 4
++        interrupt-names:
++          minItems: 4
++          maxItems: 4
++        power-domains:
